      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a general comment:\n\nThe amount of information and code duplicated across here and mk_cdisk (and libimage_aggregator, etc.) is concerning to me. I wish we have a single source of truth if possible.\n\nIn my understanding, the difficulty you faced with spawning mk_cdisk is due to the fd passing, and not because it\u0027s implemented outside of this module.\n\nSo, have you considered having a single library that implements this, and using it for both microdroid and cuttlefish? The library could be the existing C++ one (used via the cxx crate), or a new rust library based on this implementation.\n",
      "revId": "a2c650a05aacd1903ea351d374ecc2d8d312c496",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
